Local patch, not yet upstreamed: removes "sunken-server" and
"tools/brand-assets" from the workspace members list. As of commit
85436bcdd0327d21714191b19adbe98dfb9788ee both are listed but were never
actually committed (confirmed against the live GitHub repo, not just a
stale local clone) — without this patch, cargo can't resolve the workspace
manifest at all, blocking every build regardless of which package is
requested with -p. Drop this patch (or individual lines from it) once
upstream either commits the missing directories or removes the stray
member entries.

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index 0c0d300..96ea5c8 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -10,8 +10,6 @@ members = [
     "bsn-derive",
     "gateway",
     "scanner-sweep",
-    "sunken-server",
-    "tools/brand-assets",
     "tools/bsn-schema-generator",
     "tools/extract-bsn-metadata",
 ]
